          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            the conditions on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            can be divided into two steps
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                for a fixed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
                the correlators need to depend in a certain way on the choice of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+structure"} conformal structure
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ward+identities"} Ward identities
                (e.g.
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "#Gawedzki99"} Gawedzki 99, around p. 30
            %li
              %p the correlators need to glue correctly underly composition of cobordisms.
          %p
            The spaces of functionals that satisfy the first of these conditions are called
            %em conformal blocks
            \. The second condition is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sewing+constraint"} sewing constraint
            on conformal blocks.
          %p
            So conformal blocks are something like “precorrelators” or “potential correlators” of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
          %p
            The assignment of spaces of conformal blocks to surfaces and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            of these surfaces together constitutes the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} CS/WZW holography
            this is essentially the data also given by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of 3d Chern-Simons theory
            for more on this.
          %p
            From a point of view closer to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} geometric Langlands correspondence
            elements of conformal blocks are naturally thought of (
            %a{:href => "#BeauvilleLaszlo93"}> Beauville-Laszlo 93
            ) as generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+functions"} theta functions
            (see there for more).
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToBraidingOfFieldInsertions Relation to braiding of field insertions
          %p
            In the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+CFT"} rational CFT
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+category"} representation category
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebra"} vertex operator algebra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+category"} modular tensor category
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "modular+tensor+category#RepCategoriesOfVOAs"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided monoidal category
            with extra properties.
          %p
            In this case the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            (hence the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+category"} modular tensor structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+category"} representation category
            is entirely fixed by the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            (the “genus zero conformal blocks”).
          %p
            This may be found highlighted in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "modular+tensor+category#EGNO15"} EGNO 15, p. 266
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "modular+tensor+category#Runkel"} Runkel, Sec. 4.3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            of the CFT is proven in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "modular+functor#AndersenUeno12"} Andersen &amp; Ueno 2012
          %h3#holographic_correspondence Holographic correspondence
          %p
            The conformal blocks at least of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            are by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic
            correspondence given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            of 3d
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} AdS3-CFT2 and CS-WZW correspondence
          %h3#relation_to_equivariant_elliptic_cohomology Relation to equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %p
            For the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            the assignment of spaces of conformal blocks, hence by the above equivalently modular functor for
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            restricted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus-1 surfaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"}> elliptic curves
            ) is essentially what is encoded in the universal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            (equivariant
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} pre-quantum
            incarnation of the modular functor as a systems of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundles"} prequantum line bundles
            over Chern-Simons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
            (which are
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks+of+flat+connections"} moduli stacks of flat connections
            = succeed "-process" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            by forming holomorphic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            %em
              %a{:href => "equivariant+elliptic+cohomology#InterpretationInQuantumFieldTheory"} equivariant elliptic cohomology – Idea – Interpretation in Quantum field theory
            for more on this.
