          %h2#references References
          %h3#for_2d_cft For 2d CFT
          %p A review is around p. 30 of
          %ul
            %li#Gawedzki99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"}> Krzysztof Gawędzki
              ,
              %em Conformal field theory: a case study
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9904145"}> arXiv:hep-th/9904145
              )
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
          %ul
            %li#Kohno14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toshitake+Kohno"}> Toshitake Kohno
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Local Systems on Configuration Spaces, KZ Connections and Conformal Blocks
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40306-014-0088-6"} doi:10.1007/s40306-014-0088-6
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ms.u-tokyo.ac.jp/~kohno/papers/kohno_config.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toshitake+Kohno"}> Toshitake Kohno
                , §1.4 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal field theory and topology
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong 210
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-210"} AMS:mmono-210
          %p
            and via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bohr-Sommerfeld+leaves"} Bohr-Sommerfeld leaves
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Tyurin"}> Andrei Tyurin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Bohr-Sommerfeld bases
              %strong 64
              5 (2000) 1033–1064 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9909084"}> arXiv:math/9909084
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1070/IM2000v064n05ABEH000308"} doi:10.1070/IM2000v064n05ABEH000308
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathnet.ru/links/d8ad7540137cf2f33c44ab3e9455d392/im308_eng.pdf"} pdf
          %p Brief review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Wood"} Simon Wood
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang+Yang"} Yang Yang
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic structures in two-dimensional conformal field theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.02773"} arXiv:2305.02773
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+nets"} conformal nets
          %ul
            %li#BartelsDouglasHenriques14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arthur+Bartels"}> Arthur Bartels
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Douglas"} Christopher Douglas
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"} André Henriques
              %em Conformal nets II: conformal blocks
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1409.8672"}> arXiv:1409.8672
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A. Tsuchiya,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenji+Ueno"} Kenji Ueno
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal field theory on universal family of stable curves with gauge symmetries
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 19
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=92a:81191"} MR92a:81191
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenji+Ueno"}> Kenji Ueno
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal field theory with gauge symmetry
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=FIM-24"} book page
            %li
              %p
                Ratul Mahanta, Tanmoy Sengupta,
                %em Modular linear differential equations for four-point sphere conformal blocks
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.05158"}> arXiv:2211.05158
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Mikhail Pavlov,
                %em Global torus blocks in the necklace channel
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.10153"}> arXiv:2302.10153
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Vladimir Belavin, Juan Ramos Cabezas, Boris Runov:
                %em Shadow formalism for supersymmetric conformal blocks
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.07684"}> arXiv:2408.07684
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Conformal blocks for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kiyonori+Gomi"}> Kiyonori Gomi
              ,
              %em
                An analogue of the space of conformal blocks in
                = succeed "-dimensions" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 4
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (4k+2)
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.kyoto-u.ac.jp/~kgomi/papers/acb.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            In particular, argument that the higher conformal blocks of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%282%2C0%29+SCFT"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mn 6
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=6
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=(2,0)
              SCFT
            reduce to confomal blocks of the ordinary 2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            on a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
          %ul
            %li#Witten09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0905.2720.pdf#page=22"} p. 22
              of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric Langlands From Six Dimensions
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Celebration of the Mathematical Legacy of Raoul Bott
              %strong 50
              AMS (2010) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.2720"}> arXiv:0905.2720
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/crmp-50"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4777-0
          %p
            On irregular conformal blocks for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+theory"} Liouville theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
                , Joel Lamy-Poirier:
                %em
                  Irregular Singularities in the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mn 3
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3^+
                  WZW Model
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.5342"}> arXiv:1301.5342
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Babak+Haghighat"}> Babak Haghighat
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yihua+Liu"} Yihua Liu
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Reshetikhin"} Nicolai Reshetikhin
                %em Flat Connections from Irregular Conformal Blocks
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.07960"}> arXiv:2311.07960
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xia+Gu"}> Xia Gu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Babak+Haghighat"} Babak Haghighat
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Loo"} Kevin Loo
                %em Irregular Fibonacci Conformal Blocks
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.13358"}> arXiv:2311.13358
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Babak+Haghighat"}> Babak Haghighat
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Flat Connections from Irregular Conformal Blocks
                %a{:href => "CQTS#HaghighatFeb2024"} talk at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (Feb 2024) &amp;lbrack;video:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://nyu.zoom.us/rec/share/c41GdU--I_-g2XLJ7A6T0HxK6AxI-utrlGb2mStB0XBOaJ3FrvC1JzoL_FsjWrEi.MBPR87t2nBR8f99t"} zm
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://cdnapisec.kaltura.com/p/1674401/sp/167440100/embedIframeJs/uiconf_id/23435151/partner_id/1674401?iframeembed=true&playerId=kaltura_player&entry_id=1_qyu7rg1l"} kt
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Qianyu Hao,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Neitzke"} Andrew Neitzke
              %em
                A new construction of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c=1
                Virasoro blocks
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.04483"}> arXiv:2407.04483
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#relation_to_theta_functions Relation to theta functions
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+functions"} theta functions
          %ul
            %li#BeauvilleLaszlo93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Beauville"}> Arnaud Beauville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Laszlo"} Yves Laszlo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal blocks and generalized theta functions
                %strong 164
                (1994), 385 - 419,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104270837"} euclid
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9309003"} alg-geom/9309003
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1289330"} MR1289330
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Beauville"}> Arnaud Beauville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal blocks, fusion rings and the Verlinde formula
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 9
                %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~beauvill/pubs/Hirz65.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"}> Krzysztof Gawędzki
                ,
                %em Lectures on CFT
                (from Park City, published in QFT and strings for mathematicians, Dijkgraaf at al editors,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} site
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/QFT/fall/NewGaw.tex"} source
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/QFT/fall/NewGaw.dvi"} dvi
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/QFT/fall/NewGaw.ps"} ps
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"}> Alexander Beilinson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"} Yuri Manin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vadim+Schechtman"} Vadim Schechtman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sheaves of Virasoro and Neveu-Schwarz algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1289
            %li
              %p
                A.Mironov, A.Morozov, Sh.Shakirov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal blocks as Dotsenko-Fateev integral discriminants
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1001.0563"} arxiv/1001.0563
          %div
            %h3#BraidRepresentationsViaTwisteddRCohomologyOfConfigurationSpaces Braid representations via twisted cohomology of configuration spaces
            %p
              The “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypergeometric+construction+of+KZ+solutions"}> hypergeometric integral
              ” construction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
              for
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+Lie+algebra"} affine Lie algebra
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFTs"} 2d CFTs
              and of more general solutions to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+equation"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov equation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+de+Rham+cohomology"} twisted de Rham cohomology
